# Findings of the Trivy scan in the central CI pipeline that sit in npm packages bundled with the newest upstream
# release of the base image (docker.io/codercom/code-server:4.143.1; checked on Docker Hub 2026-10-24: no newer tag
# exists). They cannot be fixed here without patching code-server's own node_modules. Every entry expires on 2026-11-30:
# the build fails again then, so somebody has to look at the new upstream release. Remove entries as upstream releases
# the fixes. (The Debian packages are clean, and the unused fixuid binary was removed from the image.)

